{section}

## Error Handling and Edge Cases

### Counter System Errors

{panel:title=Error Handling Strategy|borderColor=#F44336|titleBGColor=#FFEBEE}
| Error Condition | Response | Recovery |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Shared memory unavailable** | Fatal error, restart required | Automatic on restart |
| **Counter file corruption** | Warning, use table scan recovery | Rebuild from table data |
| **Lock timeout** | Retry with backoff | Automatic retry |
| **Table limit exceeded** | Error, configuration needed | Increase max_tables |
| **Recovery timeout** | Warning, continue with incomplete data | Manual recovery trigger |
{panel}

### Edge Case Handling

{expand:title=Edge Case Management}
{code:c|title=Edge Case Handling}
// Handle counter overflow (theoretical - would take millions of years)
static uint64
handle_counter_overflow(void)
{
    if (counter_data->global_counter == UINT64_MAX)
    {
        ereport(ERROR,
                (errcode(ERRCODE_NUMERIC_VALUE_OUT_OF_RANGE),
                 errmsg("Global counter overflow"),
                 errhint("This should never happen in practice")));
    }
    return counter_data->global_counter + 1;
}

// Handle rapid table registration
static int
find_or_create_table_entry_safe(Oid table_oid)
{
    int i;
    
    // First, try to find existing entry
    for (i = 0; i < counter_data->num_tables; i++)
    {
        if (counter_data->tables[i].table_oid == table_oid)
            return i;
    }
    
    // Create new entry if space available
    if (counter_data->num_tables >= MAX_BLOCKCHAIN_TABLES)
    {
        ereport(WARNING,
                (errmsg("Maximum blockchain tables exceeded"),
                 errhint("Increase blockchain.max_tables configuration")));
        return -1;
    }
    
    // Initialize new table entry
    i = counter_data->num_tables++;
    counter_data->tables[i].table_oid = table_oid;
    counter_data->tables[i].last_counter = 0;
    counter_data->tables[i].needs_recovery = true;
    
    return i;
}
{code}
{expand}

## Security and Integrity

### Counter Security Properties

{panel:title=Security Guarantees|borderColor=#673AB7|titleBGColor=#EDE7F6}
**Uniqueness Guarantee:**
* No counter value is ever reused
* Atomic increment operations
* Transaction isolation maintained

**Integrity Properties:**
* Counter values are monotonically increasing
* No gaps in global counter sequence
* Persistence file includes checksums

**Tamper Resistance:**
* Counter values included in hash computation
* Any counter modification breaks hash chain
* File-based persistence detects corruption
{panel}

### Audit and Compliance

{expand:title=Counter Audit Capabilities}
{code:sql|title=Counter Audit Queries}
-- Verify counter sequence integrity
SELECT 
    table_name,
    COUNT(*) as total_rows,
    MIN(__tx_lsn) as min_counter,
    MAX(__tx_lsn) as max_counter,
    MAX(__tx_lsn) - MIN(__tx_lsn) + 1 as expected_count,
    CASE 
        WHEN COUNT(*) = MAX(__tx_lsn) - MIN(__tx_lsn) + 1 THEN 'VALID'
        ELSE 'GAPS_DETECTED'
    END as sequence_status
FROM audit_log
GROUP BY table_name;

-- Check for counter anomalies across tables
WITH counter_stats AS (
    SELECT 'table1' as source, __tx_lsn FROM table1
    UNION ALL
    SELECT 'table2' as source, __tx_lsn FROM table2
)
SELECT 
    source,
    COUNT(*) as row_count,
    array_agg(DISTINCT __tx_lsn ORDER BY __tx_lsn) as counter_values
FROM counter_stats
GROUP BY source
ORDER BY source;
{code}
{expand}

